# Writing guidance

You are reconstructing a {{domain}} scientific manuscript from a research
overview and prepared materials. Follow the instruction in
`/workspace/instruction.md`; this file is material guidance only.

- Ground every claim in the overview, tables, figures, and code. Do not invent
  results, citations, or experimental details.
- Report numbers exactly as given in the table/overview summaries, preserving
  units and uncertainty. Do not round or re-derive values.
- Every figure and table you reference must exist under
  `/workspace/materials/{figures,tables}/` and have an entry in the corresponding
  summary file.
- Use only citation keys present in `/workspace/materials/references.bib`.
- Distinguish your own interpretation from the source's stated findings; do not
  present inference as reported fact.
